From 505e21917c6b6d00566c779be82119eb64084777 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <parrotg9@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 17:09:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix invisible toasts, modal/title stacking, and iOS
 animation jank

Toasts
- firebase-setup.js declared `duration: 2.5`. Toastify reads that as
  milliseconds, so all 84 toasts fired from that module (every auth,
  friend, payment and validation message) were torn down 2.5ms after
  mounting and never actually rendered. Verified in a headless iPhone
  run: "Name cannot be empty" and "Amount must be a number." both fired
  with duration=2.5 and were gone before the next frame.
- Both showToast helpers now use the same values: 4s for success, 6s for
  errors, which also addresses the toasts being too short to read.

Stacking
- #TITLE was z-index 901, above the action sheet's backdrop (850) and
  dock (900). With the add/clear sheet open the "TABS" heading stayed
  sharp and fully lit on top of the blurred overlay. Dropped to 100,
  which is all it needs to clear the logo (98) and menu button (99).
- #editMoneyModal set z-index 50, overriding the 9999 it already gets
  from the shared modal rule (same specificity, later in the file). The
  Add/Remove Money modal rendered behind the action dock and the title.
  Removed the override so it stacks with every other modal.

iOS animation smoothness
The iOS app is a WKWebView over the site, so these are the app's
animations too.
- The side nav transitioned `backdrop-filter` from blur(0) to blur(8px),
  forcing a full-screen gaussian blur recomputation on every frame of
  the 0.4s open. The blur is now static on a ::before layer and only its
  opacity animates, which the compositor handles on the GPU.
- The side nav panel animated `width` 0 -> 250px, relaying out and
  re-wrapping the text of every nav link each frame. It now slides on a
  composited transform at a fixed width.
- Modal backdrops transitioned backdrop-filter alongside their opacity
  fade; the opacity animation already fades the blur, so the separate
  blur transition was redundant per-frame work.
- Dropped `.sidenav`'s bare `transition: 0.5s` (shorthand for `all`),
  which fought the transform transition and animated paint-only props.
- Added will-change / backface-visibility hints on the elements that
  actually animate, and momentum scrolling inside the open action sheet.

Animation durations are unchanged, so the *_ANIM_MS constants in
script.js still line up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BjNa7gE55zpGkwR8JN3x2U
---
 firebase-setup.js |  6 ++++-
 script.js         |  3 ++-
 styles.css        | 64 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 3 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/firebase-setup.js b/firebase-setup.js
index 8e9fb9d..b9ab6c0 100644
--- a/firebase-setup.js
+++ b/firebase-setup.js
@@ -62,7 +62,11 @@ const firebaseConfig = {
 function showToast(message, type = "success") {
   Toastify({
     text: `${message}`, // Prepend icon to message
-    duration: 2.5,
+    // Milliseconds. This used to read `2.5`, which Toastify took literally —
+    // every toast in this file was removed 2.5ms after it mounted, i.e. it
+    // never actually rendered. Errors linger longer than successes since
+    // they carry something the user has to read and act on.
+    duration: type === "error" ? 6000 : 4000,
     close: true,
     gravity: "top",
     position: "right",
diff --git a/script.js b/script.js
index a7a21ad..6a1f19f 100644
--- a/script.js
+++ b/script.js
@@ -3,7 +3,8 @@
 function showToast(message, type = "success") {
   Toastify({
     text: `${message}`,
-    duration: 2500,
+    // Keep these in step with the showToast in firebase-setup.js.
+    duration: type === "error" ? 6000 : 4000,
     close: true,
     gravity: "top",
     position: "right",
diff --git a/styles.css b/styles.css
index 9c40208..9799c1b 100644
--- a/styles.css
+++ b/styles.css
@@ -36,7 +36,11 @@ body {
   top: calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-top));
