From a04aa1129de6ee015f08387db1a31d0bfeeb90c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <parrotg9@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 17:10:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Give the React Native toast the same readable duration as
 the web
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mobile/ is the second iOS target (bundleIdentifier com.tabsonfriends.app)
and had the same complaint as the web app: toasts vanished after 2.2s.
They are rendered pointerEvents:"none", so there is no way to dismiss one
early or hold it open — it has to stay up long enough to be read.

Matches the web showToast now: 4s for success, 6s for errors.

The rest of the RN app's animation surface is already smooth — the only
Animated usage is this toast's opacity fade (already on the native
driver), and ModalCard defers to the platform Modal's native "fade".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BjNa7gE55zpGkwR8JN3x2U
---
 mobile/src/context/ToastContext.js | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mobile/src/context/ToastContext.js b/mobile/src/context/ToastContext.js
index 7adfd6f..11e8fc2 100644
--- a/mobile/src/context/ToastContext.js
+++ b/mobile/src/context/ToastContext.js
@@ -19,13 +19,16 @@ export function ToastProvider({ children }) {
       useNativeDriver: true,
     }).start();
 
+    // Matches the web showToast (4s / 6s). These toasts are pointerEvents:
+    // "none", so there is no way to dismiss one early — it has to stay up long
+    // enough to actually be read.
     hideTimer.current = setTimeout(() => {
       Animated.timing(opacity, {
         toValue: 0,
         duration: 200,
         useNativeDriver: true,
       }).start(() => setToast(null));
-    }, 2200);
+    }, type === "error" ? 6000 : 4000);
   }, [opacity]);
 
   return (
